**🟡 Warning - Best Practice: Missing Event Listener Cleanup (Memory Leak)**

**File:** `app/javascript/controllers/nik_edit_controller.js` (lines 886-933)

**Problem:**
Stimulus controller adds event listener in `connect()` but doesn't remove it in `disconnect()`, causing potential memory leaks.

```javascript
export default class extends Controller {
  connect() {
    this.nikInput = this.element.querySelector("#customer_nik")
    if (!this.nikInput) return
    this.originalNikValue = this.nikInput.value
    this.createCheckNikButton()

    // Event listener added but never removed
    this.nikInput.addEventListener("input", this.checkValue.bind(this))
  }

  // ❌ NO disconnect() method
}
```

**Why This Matters:**
- If the controller is destroyed and recreated multiple times (popup opened/closed repeatedly), event listeners accumulate
- Can cause performance degradation over time
- Dynamically created DOM elements (checkButton) aren't cleaned up

**Suggested Fix:**

```javascript
export default class extends Controller {
  connect() {
    this.nikInput = this.element.querySelector("#customer_nik")
    if (!this.nikInput) return

    this.originalNikValue = this.nikInput.value
    this.createCheckNikButton()

    // Store bound function reference for cleanup
    this.boundCheckValue = this.checkValue.bind(this)
    this.nikInput.addEventListener("input", this.boundCheckValue)
  }

  disconnect() {
    // Clean up event listeners
    if (this.nikInput && this.boundCheckValue) {
      this.nikInput.removeEventListener("input", this.boundCheckValue)
    }

    // Remove dynamically created button
    if (this.checkButton && this.checkButton.parentElement) {
      this.checkButton.remove()
    }

    // Clear references
    this.nikInput = null
    this.checkButton = null
    this.boundCheckValue = null
  }

  checkValue() {
    if (this.nikInput.value !== this.originalNikValue) {
      this.checkButton.style.display = 'flex'
    } else {
      this.checkButton.style.display = 'none'
    }
  }
}
```

**Recommendation:** Always implement `disconnect()` lifecycle method to clean up event listeners and DOM modifications.

